From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:00:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 48/48] hottyterm: a backdrop bleeds to the window's edges
 (V6-06)

A backdrop that reaches an edge of the grid goes on to the window's edge,
over the padding and the pixels left over when the window isn't a whole
number of cells. Without it, a program that cards its panes on a
backdrop the size of the screen still shows the terminal's background in
a strip along the bottom and the right: at 1.6 in a 2874x1845 window,
55 rows of 33 pixels and 191 columns of 15 leave 30 pixels below the
grid and 9 to its right, whatever the backdrop draws.

The strips are the backdrop's outermost pixels: past each edge it
reaches, a quad sampling the middle of its last row or column, and in a
corner its corner pixel, so they are those pixels' colour exactly. Only
hotty backdrops bleed: a surface's image (hotty's image ids) below
kitty's line for images under the backgrounds. A program's own kitty
image there draws as before. A cell that paints its background still
covers the padding beside it with window-padding-color = extend, since
the cells' backgrounds draw after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/renderer/generic.zig |  14 +++
 src/renderer/image.zig   | 254 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 src/termio/hotty.zig     |  25 ++++
 3 files changed, 256 insertions(+), 37 deletions(-)

